# libpdx-schema-registry — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R90-XREPO.012 (svc.schema-registry stand-up)
# Doc:  paideia-os → design/round-retrospectives/r90-xrepo-wave3-plan.md §4
#
# libpdx-schema-registry is a client-side shared library. Its M2 API
# surface (schema_register / schema_lookup / schema_list) is a pure
# in-process catalog operating on caller-owned memory — no syscalls, no
# capability grants required from the consumer.
#
# M3 layers in three optional cross-library dependencies (see
# deps.list). The relevant capability surface at that point is inherited
# from the sibling libraries the consumer links:
#
#   * libpdx-audit — needs KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(write, svc.audit-journal)
#     via svc_lookup, if the consumer wants the audit hook (M3-001) to
#     actually publish. libpdx-schema-registry itself only reads
#     AuditRecord::record_state as a client-side D3 / I5 gate.
#
#   * libpdx-elevate — needs KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(write, svc.elevate-
#     broker) via svc_lookup, if the consumer wants to acquire the
#     R_SCHEMA_REGISTER grant that arms the M3-002 gate.
#
#   * libpdx-semantic-pipe — needs KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(write,
#     svc.schema-registry) via svc_lookup, if the consumer wants the
#     M3-003 wire path to forward register / lookup ops to the kernel
#     daemon rather than only maintaining a local catalog.
#
# At M2 (this milestone): no requires: line — the library issues zero
# syscalls of its own. declares_output_schemas: is added at M3-001 when
# the audit hook lands.
